        <groundspeak:log id="346505647">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-08-31T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1985141">rat root</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 419 Cardinal divide&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The weather was perfect for the hike to this cap with Crafty nana, Caren Bear, myself and 3 dogs. We met a number of hikers who went as far as cardinal cap. We even had the privilege of witnessing a young couple proposing for marriage with the gift of an engagement ring on the ridge. When we got close to the cairn the dogs went crazy for what we believe was a marmot inside the cairn.

Thanks OFTH for this cap at a place that has lots of memory's for me.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="346095523">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-08-31T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3867146">Crafty nana</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 419

Cardinal Divide&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rat root, carenbear and myself went up to the Cardinal Divide today and walked the ridge to the Brass Cap and also picked up sleepy hollow's cache there. What a view. Best day of the year for this walk. So glad we came here. Thanks so much for posting the cap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rat root will send in the information for this one for me.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="346093635">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-08-31T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7994819">Caren Bear</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 419 Cardinal Divide &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;rat root and crafty mama have introduced me to geocaching and now here we are up on the Cardinal Divide next to Sleepy Hollow's cache we find this brass cap - rat root will send the info&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="326380332">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-06-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP419 – Cardinal Divide

Posted Coords: N52 54.518 W117 11.507

My GPSr: N52 54.517 W117 11.516 (10m out!)

My Elevation: 2148 m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cap and S_H's nearby cache were my main goals today. I'd seen the pics of past finders and the area looked like such a great place to experience. It certainly didn't disappoint. The weather was perfect as I made the short climb up the top of the ridge and started the trek over to the cap – a cotton t-shirt was all I needed in the warm sun. On the way along the ridge I encountered a herd of humans and gradually overtook them (I think their foraging for photographs slowed them down a bit) and in the end the cap site was much further than they were going, so I had the whole place to myself by the time I reached ground zero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This one is different to be sure, so much so that I honestly wondered if I'd found the right thing. The shred of doubt lingered because my coords were about 10m out on this one; while finding S-H's nearby cache they were bang on. A little further along the ridge I saw another marker post and checked it out, finding it to be second coal company marker found today – the other is easily seen beside a marker on the way to this cap – er – marker thingy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I had a lot of fun making my way here and taking ample pictures of the ridge and the valley to the north and the impressive range of mountains to the south. I must have taken about 40 of the same shots of this unique ridge – at least one of those should be a keeper, right?.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for luring me out here. I honestly wouldn't have discovered this excellent spot if it hadn't been for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
